## Description

The Omni (chat input window) grew inconsistently and clipped input lines — most visibly when pasting text quickly or cycling through input history, leaving lines half cut off.

**Root cause:** `getRowHeight()` derived the window height from `widget.contentHeight`, which is backed by a ResizeObserver and lags a frame behind. `layout()` re-lays the editor synchronously, but then read that stale (smaller) height to size the window, clipping newly-added lines until the observer caught up.

- **Synchronous height measurement:** `getRowHeight()` now reads `widget.input.element.offsetHeight` (the same container the ResizeObserver watches) instead of the lagging `widget.contentHeight` observable, so the window grows in lockstep with the editor's synchronous layout.

```ts
// before: ResizeObserver-backed, stale during synchronous layout
let contentHeight = Math.ceil(widget.contentHeight);
// after: synchronous, matches the just-laid-out editor
let contentHeight = Math.ceil(widget.input.element.offsetHeight);
```

